{"id": "en_story_hudson", "tag": "AVIATION", "cta": "MORE TRUE STORIES LIKE THIS", "ctaSmall": "follow", "ctaWhere": "new story every day", "accent": "#4FC3F7", "lang": "en", "total": 72.79, "segments": [{"text": "An Airbus A320 carrying 155 people suddenly loses all engine power over New York City.", "start": 0.0, "end": 6.06}, {"text": "On 15 January 2009, US Airways Flight 1549 takes off from LaGuardia airport as planned.", "start": 6.54, "end": 12.46}, {"text": "At about 2,800 feet, the aircraft strikes a flock of Canada geese without any advance warning.", "start": 13.06, "end": 18.04}, {"text": "Both engines lose all thrust immediately, leaving the passenger plane gliding in absolute sky silence.", "start": 18.62, "end": 20.636}, {"text": "Captain Chesley 'Sully' Sullenberger and first officer Jeffrey Skiles immediately take control of the situation.", "start": 24.6, "end": 29.14}, {"text": "The pilot crew quickly decides that they cannot reach any airport from their current position.", "start": 29.72, "end": 33.06}, {"text": "They have less than 4 minutes from the initial bird strike to make their move.", "start": 33.46, "end": 36.68}, {"text": "They decide to land on the Hudson River right near Midtown Manhattan in New York.", "start": 37.1, "end": 40.76}, {"text": "The pilots bring the heavy Airbus A320 down onto the surface of the open river.", "start": 41.56, "end": 44.92}, {"text": "NY Waterway ferries arrive at the landing spot within minutes to assist all the survivors.", "start": 45.66, "end": 49.44}, {"text": "Against all impossible odds, every single one of the 155 people on board safely survives.", "start": 50.26, "end": 55.12}, {"text": "The entire event takes less than 4 minutes from bird strike to total final safety.", "start": 56.22, "end": 60.18}, {"text": "Quick actions by Captain Chesley 'Sully' Sullenberger and Jeffrey Skiles save all 155 human lives.", "start": 60.74, "end": 65.9}, {"text": "Would you remain completely calm if your plane l